N5008 [temp.deduct.type]/8: the partial specialization pattern T C::*
deduces both the member type and the class from a pointer-to-member argument
(libstdc++ __result_of_memfun<_Res _Class::*, ...>), and does NOT match a
plain pointer; pointer-to-member instances get distinct names (memptr_C_T)
so memfun<int S::*> and memfun<int*> are different instantiations.
